# `xs.each.<field>` and `xs.each.<method>(…)`: a field or method of every item, the list's own field unchanged
# (decision each-field-broadcast, card xs-each)
'xs = ["ab", "c"]; xs.each.count'	[2, 1]
'class Counter{count: int}; counters = [Counter{count: 2}, Counter{count: 5}]; sum(counters.each.count)'	7
'xs = ["abc", "cde"]; xs.each.contains("c")'	[yes, yes]
'xs = ["ab", "c"]; xs.count'	2

# the explicit broadcast maps any function, a library word's too (decision each-all-broadcast)
'xs = ["a", "bb"]; count each xs'	[1, 2]
'abs all [-1, 2]'	[1, 2]

# `xs.each {…}`: the block applied to every item, the list of its results, as map gives it (decision each-maps)
'[1, 2, 3].each{it * 2}'	[2, 4, 6]
'xs = [1, 2, 3]; xs.each {it + 1}'	[2, 3, 4]
